 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n### Issue: Unexpected Behavior in `get_or_add` Method of `Relationships` Class\n\n#### Description\nI've encountered an issue with the `get_or_add` method in the `Relationships` class. It seems that the method is not behaving as expected when attempting to find or add a relationship. This behavior was observed after recent changes to the `_next_rId` method.\n\n#### Environment\n- **Python Version**: 3.10.15\n- **Operating System**: Linux\n- **pytest Version**: 8.3.4\n- **Plugins**: xdist-3.6.1, cov-6.0.0\n\n#### Steps to Reproduce\nHere's a minimal example to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nfrom docx.opc.rel import Relationships\n\ndef test_get_or_add_relationship():\n    rels = Relationships()\n    reltype = \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/image\"\n    part = \"image1.png\"\n    \n    # Attempt to get or add a relationship\n    relationship = rels.get_or_add(reltype, part)\n    \n    # Check if the relationship is correctly added\n    assert relationship.reltype == reltype\n    assert relationship.target_part == part\n\ntest_get_or_add_relationship()\n```\n\n#### Expected Behavior\nThe `get_or_add` method should return the existing relationship if it exists, or add a new one if it doesn't. The returned relationship should match the specified `reltype` and `part`.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\nThe method does not return the expected relationship object, leading to assertion failures.\n\n#### Additional Information\nThis issue seems to have surfaced after the recent changes to the `_next_rId` method, which might be affecting the generation of new relationship IDs. Any insights or suggestions for a workaround would be appreciated.\n</issue>\n",
